ule, keep yibao (basic medical insurance) active, and plan job searches methodically — don’t just stay at home all day"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"People who lose a loved one to suicide, accident, or homicide should seek professional help rather than trying to cope alone"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"In the first six months after losing a spouse, assign one trusted person to oversee meals, sleep, medication for chronic conditions, and follow‑up appointments"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"For those without family or friends, replace “the person watching over you” with three simple things: a neighbor who can enter your home, a spot on the community outreach list, and emergency contacts saved on your phone"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"After a parent dies, tell the child the truth, let him attend the funeral, and don’t send him to another environment"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Still stuck in grief after half a year, unable to move on — when to see a psychiatrist or clinical psychologist"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Don’t spend money on grief counseling right away — first check whether your grief is truly stuck (see the symptoms listed in item 8)"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Don’t drop yibao or turn to alcohol after separating or divorcing"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Call 12356 for general support, 12355 for minors and teens; for medical care, book a psychology clinic appointment"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"In the first three months after a tragedy, postpone any irreversible major decisions"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Don’t treat death as a way to settle debts: life insurance won’t pay out for suicides within two years, workplace injuries won’t be recognized, and debts are still deducted from your estate first"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/29"},"children":["Chapter 29"," ·"," ","After experiencing a major setback"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"29-01"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["01"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["After a loved one passes, don’t stay alone for the first few days. Those with heart disease, high blood pressure, or diabetes should keep taking their medication. If you feel pressure or pain in the chest, call 120 right away"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["In the first day after losing a loved one, the risk of a heart attack is about 21.1 times higher than normal, then it drops each day afterward. For people aged 60 to 89, the rate of heart attacks or strokes within 30 days of losing a spouse roughly doubles compared to the general population, then returns to normal after a month. Those already dealing with heart disease must not skip their medication. Chest pressure, shortness of breath, or weakness in one arm or leg are clear emergency signs — call 120 immediately."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no cost involved. Just avoid being alone during t…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["This conclusion comes from a study of 1,985 acute heart attack patients, comparing their health status before…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: After a loved one passes, don’t stay alone for the first few days. Those with heart disease, high blood pressure, or diabetes should keep taking their medication. If you feel pressure or pain in the chest, call 120 right away"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no cost involved. Just avoid being alone during these days and keep taking your medicine as usual."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["This conclusion comes from a study of 1,985 acute heart attack patients, comparing their health status before and after the event. Out of them, 270 individuals (13.6%) had lost someone close within six months prior, and 19 lost a loved one just one day before the attack. Within 24 hours of such a loss, the risk of a heart attack rose 21.1 times (95% CI 13.1–34.1; actual range roughly 13 to 34 times). This risk then gradually decreased day by day. To put this into perspective: among people with a baseline 5% ten-year risk of heart attack, one extra case occurs for every 1,394 people who recently lost a loved one; for those with a 20% baseline risk, the figure is one extra case per 320 people. Another UK-based study compared 30,447 widowed individuals aged 60–89 with 83,588 similar controls. Within 30 days of bereavement, 0.16% of the bereaved group suffered a heart attack or stroke, versus 0.08% of controls — an IRR of 2.20 (1.52–3.15), meaning their risk was roughly 2.2 times higher. Specifically, heart attack risk was 2.14 times higher (1.20–3.81) and stroke risk 2.40 times higher (1.22–4.71). These elevated risks faded after 30 days. Over 90 days, two other conditions also showed increased risk: acute coronary syndrome (IRR 2.20, 1.12–4.29) and pulmonary embolism (IRR 2.37, 1.18–4.75). In total, 67 people in the control group experienced such events, and the heart attack risk was 2.1 times higher for bereaved individuals."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["Mostofsky E, et al. (2012). Risk of acute myocardial infarction after the death of a significant person in one's life: the Determinants of Myocardial Infarction Onset Study. Circulation. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.111.061770","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.111.061770"]},"；Carey IM, et al. (2014). Increased risk of acute cardiovascular events after partner bereavement: a matched cohort study. JAMA Internal Medicine. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamainternmed.2013.14558","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1001/jamainternmed.2013.14558"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.111.061770","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["Practical steps are easy to follow: ask someone else to manage your medication rather than relying on memory alone. Avoid long-distance travel during this period, and do not try to cope by drinking alcohol — details on alcohol’s effects are covered in Section 2. Recognizing heart attacks and strokes, plus instructions on calling emergency services, are explained in Section 13. Both studies referenced here rely on retrospective population data, so it’s hard to determine exactly how many participants would have developed these conditions anyway. Yet both studies point to the same general trend and timeframe. For anyone unable to arrange help or who must remain alone during these days, please see point 6 in this section."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[]},{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link next","href":"/en/tip/29-02"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Next"]},"On the week you receive a cancer diagnosis, don’t go alone to pick up the results — postpone non‑treatment decisions"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M5 12h14"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"section","props":{"className":"life-tip-related"},"children":[{"tag":"h2","props":{},"children":["More in th